name:Adoro te devote;
office-part:Hymnus;
book:Cantus varii romano-seraphici, 1902, p. 97;
transcriber:Christopher Tatum;
%%
(cb3)JE[O Jesus, whom veiled now I see,](h)SU,(h) quem(g) ve(f)lá(f)tum(g) nunc(f) a(h)spí(h)ci(i)o,(h) (;) 
O[I pray it may be which I so thirst for](h)ro,(g) fi(f)at(f) il(h)lud(f) quod(e) tam(d) sí(f)ti(e)o:(d) (:) 
Ut[That, thee unveiled beholding](h) te(f) re(g)ve(h)lá(i)ta(h) cer(g)nens(f) fá[face](h)ci(g)e,(f) (;) 
Vi[By sight I may be blessed of thy glory](h)su(f) sim(g) be(h)á(i)tus(h) tu(g)æ(f) gló(efe)ri(d)æ.(d) (::)
A[Hail Jesus, shepherd of the faithful](k)ve(j) Je(i)su!(h) (,) Pa(h)stor(g) fi(f)dé(h)li(g)um,(f) (;) 
Ad(h)aú[Increase faith of all](h)ge(f) fi(g)dem(h) óm(i)ni(h)um(h) (;) 
In[In thee believing](f) te(g) cre(f)dén(e)ti(d)um.(d) (::)
A(ded)men.(cd) (::)
